.TH SDL_AudioDeviceEvent 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_AudioDeviceEvent \- Audio device event structure (event.adevice.*)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_events.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef struct SDL_AudioDeviceEvent
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_EventType type; /**< SDL_EVENT_AUDIO_DEVICE_ADDED, or SDL_EVENT_AUDIO_DEVICE_REMOVED, or SDL_EVENT_AUDIO_DEVICE_FORMAT_CHANGED */
.BI "    Uint32 reserved;
.BI "    Uint64 timestamp;   /**< In nanoseconds, populated using SDL_GetTicksNS() */
.BI "    SDL_AudioDeviceID which;       /**< SDL_AudioDeviceID for the device being added or removed or changing */
.BI "    bool recording; /**< false if a playback device, true if a recording device. */
.BI "    Uint8 padding1;
.BI "    Uint8 padding2;
.BI "    Uint8 padding3;
.BI "} SDL_AudioDeviceEvent;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Note that SDL will send a
.BR SDL_EVENT_AUDIO_DEVICE_ADDED
event for every device it discovers during initialization\[char46] After that, this event will only arrive when a device is hotplugged during the program\(aqs run\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This struct is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

